WEBVTT

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.237
In this short

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:07.207
film, you will learn about
how your urinary system works,

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.176
the different parts of your body
that are involved,

00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:12.579
and the different functions
they each have.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.948
The urinary system filters and excretes
waste,

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:18.418
and it's made up of two parts.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.787
The upper urinary system
includes the kidneys

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:24.825
and ureters.

00:00:24.825 --> 00:00:26.593
The kidneys filter your blood of excess

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:32.265
fluid and impurities,
which then become urine.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.167
The ureters are tubes that transport

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.237
urine from the kidneys to the bladder.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.873
There is a valve within
the ureters that prevents urine back

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.475
flowing to the kidneys.

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:50.350
The backflow of urine
could cause damage to the kidneys.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.585
The lower urinary system

00:00:51.585 --> 00:00:55.489
includes the bladder,
the urethra and the sphincter muscles.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:59.726
The adult male urethra is somewhere
between 18 to 20 centimeters long.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:03.964
It's the tube between the bladder
and the opening of the urethra.

00:01:03.964 --> 00:01:06.099
Right below
the bladder, where the urethra starts

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:09.369
is an internal sphincter muscle
and the prostate

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:14.441
gland.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.475
The bladder is a hollow,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:18.879
muscular
organ made up of several muscle layers.

00:01:18.879 --> 00:01:22.649
The bladders main function is to store
and eliminate urine.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.917
The bladder receives signals

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.920
as it fills with urine to indicate
the need to urinate.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.056
When the bladder is about halfway
full, around 250

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:33.460
milliliters, you get the first sensation
you need to urinate.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.928
As the bladder continues to fill,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:39.166
the sensation becomes stronger
and the urgency to urinate increases.

00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:43.370
The bladder muscles relax as your bladder
fills, but contract when you urinate.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.406
The sphincter muscle controls
the flow of urine out of the bladder,

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:49.776
which squeezes the urethra shut
as the bladder fills and relaxes.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:54.414
As the bladder is emptied.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.248
To summarize,

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.450
the urinary
system is made up of two parts,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.353
which includes the upper and lower system,
and both play

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:04.353
an important role in the production
and excretion of urine from the body.
